# Branch Node

**Schema `node_type`:** `branch`

## Documentation

{{{docs_branch}}}

## Branch Structure

A branch node uses the `branches` array at the node level (not inside `properties`).
Each branch has 2-10 items: up to 9 conditional branches and 1 default branch (must be last).

### Branch item properties

{{schema-table (get branch_schema "$definitions.temp_branch.items")}}

### Condition expression operators

{{schema-enum (get fragment_schema "$definitions.condition_expr_v1_branch_def.properties.expression_v1.properties.args.items.properties.op.enum")}}

### Variable namespaces (in branch conditions)

{{schema-enum (get fragment_schema "$definitions.condition_expr_v1_branch_def.properties.expression_v1.properties.args.items.properties.variable_ns.enum")}}

## Example

```json
{
  "node_type": "branch",
  "properties": {},
  "branches": [
    {
      "name": "Premium users",
      "is_default": false,
      "conditions": [
        {
          "type": "expression_v1",
          "expression_v1": {
            "op": "AND",
            "args": [
              { "variable_ns": "$recipient", "variable": "plan", "op": "==", "value": "premium" }
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "nodes": [
        { "node_type": "send_smart_channel_routing", "properties": { "template": "premium-alert" } }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Default",
      "is_default": true,
      "conditions": [{ "type": "expression_v1", "expression_v1": { "op": "AND", "args": [] } }],
      "nodes": [
        { "node_type": "send_email", "properties": { "template": "free-tier-alert" } }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```
